1
00:00:02,660 --> 00:00:05,580
Okay, this one's rare. This one is medium well. Go!

2
00:00:05,750 --> 00:00:07,710
Hey, Phoebe! How was dinner?

3
00:00:05,750 --> 00:00:07,710
Hey!

4
00:00:07,880 --> 00:00:10,460
Dinner was good! Just saying hi! Now I'm gonna go!

5
00:00:10,630 --> 00:00:12,380
All right, okay.

6
00:00:12,550 --> 00:00:15,970
Oh. Well, hello there.

7
00:00:12,550 --> 00:00:15,970
Hi.

8
00:00:16,140 --> 00:00:18,760
I didn't see this on the menu.

9
00:00:18,930 --> 00:00:21,220
Tim,this is Phoebe, Phoebe, this is Tim, my new sous chef.

10
00:00:21,390 --> 00:00:24,730
Oh. So you're Monica's boss?

11
00:00:21,390 --> 00:00:24,730
Actually, she's my boss.

12
00:00:24,890 --> 00:00:29,440
"Sous" is French for "under."

13
00:00:24,890 --> 00:00:29,440
Ah! I "sous-stand." Heh.

14
00:00:29,610 --> 00:00:33,030
Tim, I need a calamari and a caesar salad. And could you get me the pesto?

15
00:00:33,190 --> 00:00:35,200
Yeah.

16
00:00:33,190 --> 00:00:35,200
You made pesto?

17
00:00:35,360 --> 00:00:36,570
Yes, I did.

18
00:00:36,740 --> 00:00:39,870
Would you say your pesto is the best-o? Heh.

19
00:00:40,040 --> 00:00:42,620
I don't know. I would say it's pretty good-o.

20
00:00:46,040 --> 00:00:48,040
I still need the calamari and the salad.

21
00:00:48,210 --> 00:00:50,380
I like your necklace.

22
00:00:48,210 --> 00:00:50,380
Oh, I made it myself.

23
00:00:50,550 --> 00:00:53,840
You are so talented.

24
00:00:50,550 --> 00:00:53,840
Well, it's no pesto.

25
00:00:55,300 --> 00:00:58,930
All right, let's just cut to the chase. Okay? You're single, you're single.

26
00:00:59,100 --> 00:01:01,970
He gets off work at 11. She'll be waiting for your call.

27
00:01:02,140 --> 00:01:07,480
I'll give him your number if I could just get calamari and caesar salad!

28
00:01:09,060 --> 00:01:11,900
I did not yell. I am not putting a dollar in the jar.

29
00:01:55,110 --> 00:01:59,950
Wow, Bing! Burning the midnight oil.

30
00:01:55,110 --> 00:01:59,950
You know me, sir.

31
00:02:00,120 --> 00:02:03,780
Oh, I have a question. Do you know how can I get around the computer network...

32
00:02:03,950 --> 00:02:06,910
...so I can access the really good Internet porn?

33
00:02:08,290 --> 00:02:10,330
You're a joker, Bing.

34
00:02:11,960 --> 00:02:14,460
What's funny about that?

35
00:02:14,840 --> 00:02:18,470
Sorry I kept you waiting so long.

36
00:02:14,840 --> 00:02:18,470
That's okay. Where do you wanna go?

37
00:02:18,630 --> 00:02:21,640
Oh, uh, I think you know where I wanna go.

38
00:02:21,800 --> 00:02:24,390
The Hard Rock Cafe?

39
00:02:21,800 --> 00:02:24,390
Yeah.

40
00:02:24,560 --> 00:02:26,180
Again?

41
00:02:24,560 --> 00:02:26,180
Yeah.

42
00:02:28,310 --> 00:02:32,690
I'm telling you, I like the food.

43
00:02:28,310 --> 00:02:32,690
You like the Purple Rain display.

44
00:02:34,360 --> 00:02:37,690
Hey, Bob.

45
00:02:34,360 --> 00:02:37,690
Hey, Toby. Have a good night.

46
00:02:38,530 --> 00:02:43,570
Did that guy just call you Toby?

47
00:02:38,530 --> 00:02:43,570
Yeah, he thinks that's my name.

48
00:02:44,370 --> 00:02:48,700
Why don't you correct him?

49
00:02:44,370 --> 00:02:48,700
Oh, it's been way too long now.

50
00:02:48,960 --> 00:02:52,290
The first time, we were passing each other so I didn't say anything.

51
00:02:52,460 --> 00:02:55,880
The next time he said, "Hey, Toby, want a doughnut?"

52
00:02:56,050 --> 00:02:59,380
And I wanted the doughnut.

53
00:02:59,550 --> 00:03:03,510
Five years later, the doughnut's gone and I'm still Toby.

54
00:03:03,680 --> 00:03:07,850
Five years? Chandler, you have to tell him.

55
00:03:03,680 --> 00:03:07,850
No, that would be so awkward.

56
00:03:08,020 --> 00:03:11,140
Besides, we work in different departments. He's on the sixth floor.

57
00:03:11,310 --> 00:03:14,440
So he calls me Toby once in a while. Big deal. Could be worse.

58
00:03:14,610 --> 00:03:17,440
It's not like he's calling me Muriel.

59
00:03:17,690 --> 00:03:21,780
Muriel. Why would he call you Muriel?

60
00:03:25,780 --> 00:03:26,990
Oh, my God.

61
00:03:28,910 --> 00:03:31,460
Chandler M. Bing.

62
00:03:33,670 --> 00:03:37,250
It's not just an M. Your middle name is Muriel!

63
00:03:37,420 --> 00:03:40,550
Shh! It is a family name.

64
00:03:41,510 --> 00:03:45,390
Chandler Muriel Bing.

65
00:03:45,550 --> 00:03:48,010
Your parents never even gave you a chance, did they?

66
00:03:51,270 --> 00:03:54,440
Drake, I've discovered the reason for your headaches and memory loss.

67
00:03:54,600 --> 00:03:55,690
What is it?

68
00:03:55,860 --> 00:03:59,070
Apparently, your brain transplant was not entirely successful.

69
00:03:59,230 --> 00:04:01,900
It seems your body is rejecting Jessica's brain.

70
00:04:02,070 --> 00:04:04,320
Is it serious?

71
00:04:04,490 --> 00:04:06,990
Not if we extract tissue from the original body...

72
00:04:07,160 --> 00:04:09,910
...synthesize antibodies, introduce them into your system...

73
00:04:10,080 --> 00:04:13,080
...which could stop you from rejecting the brain.

74
00:04:13,250 --> 00:04:16,960
That sounds simple enough. Let's just do that.

75
00:04:17,130 --> 00:04:20,960
We would, but when we went to exhume Jessica's body...

76
00:04:21,130 --> 00:04:23,550
...it was gone.

77
00:04:26,300 --> 00:04:29,140
Cut. Very nice, people.

78
00:04:29,310 --> 00:04:31,680
Let me change and we can go to dinner.

79
00:04:29,310 --> 00:04:31,680
Wh...? Oh.

80
00:04:31,850 --> 00:04:36,310
What happened to Jessica's body?

81
00:04:31,850 --> 00:04:36,310
I'm not telling. You'll have to see it on TV.

82
00:04:36,480 --> 00:04:39,480
You don't know, do you?

83
00:04:36,480 --> 00:04:39,480
No. Couldn't care less.

84
00:04:40,110 --> 00:04:42,650
Hey, good scene, man. All right.

85
00:04:40,110 --> 00:04:42,650
You too.

86
00:04:46,450 --> 00:04:49,200
What? You weren't in it.

87
00:04:50,160 --> 00:04:54,250
Oh, sorry. Uh, Kash, this is my friend Rachel. Rachel, Kash.

88
00:04:54,410 --> 00:04:57,420
Hi.

89
00:04:54,410 --> 00:04:57,420
How come I haven't seen you here before?

90
00:04:57,580 --> 00:05:01,250
Well, heh. Joey probably just thinks I'll embarrass him.

91
00:05:01,420 --> 00:05:04,670
He thinks I'm some kind of soap opera nut. Ha-ha-ha.

92
00:05:04,840 --> 00:05:07,300
Which I'm not. I'm not. Ha, ha.

93
00:05:07,470 --> 00:05:11,310
Although, I do know your favorite ice cream flavor is butter pecan.

94
00:05:12,850 --> 00:05:16,060
And, uh... And your dog's name is Wally.

95
00:05:17,980 --> 00:05:20,940
Look at that, I'm just stroking your arm.

96
00:05:17,980 --> 00:05:20,940
Here we go.

97
00:05:21,110 --> 00:05:24,110
We're leaving. Bye, Kash. Say hi to Wally.

98
00:05:28,820 --> 00:05:30,620
Oh, Monica.

99
00:05:28,820 --> 00:05:30,620
Hi.

100
00:05:30,780 --> 00:05:35,750
Oh, my God, I had the best time with Tim last night. He is so sweet.

101
00:05:35,910 --> 00:05:38,460
Ugh! I can't wait to get "sous-neath" him.

102
00:05:39,790 --> 00:05:42,590
Uh, I... I have to fire him.

103
00:05:39,790 --> 00:05:42,590
Why?

104
00:05:42,750 --> 00:05:46,170
Because He's terrible. He's slow. He burns things.

105
00:05:46,340 --> 00:05:48,970
Last night he lit my pastry chef on fire.

106
00:05:49,140 --> 00:05:52,510
He was nervous. You can be very intimidating.

107
00:05:52,680 --> 00:05:56,520
And I've met your pastry chef. She can stand to be taken down a peg.

108
00:05:56,680 --> 00:06:00,060
Well, now she has no eyebrows. Mission accomplished.

109
00:06:00,810 --> 00:06:04,020
But Monica, he loves his job so much.

110
00:06:04,190 --> 00:06:07,150
Can't you just give him another chance, please?

111
00:06:09,320 --> 00:06:12,490
All right. But if he lights someone else on fire, he is out of there.

112
00:06:12,660 --> 00:06:16,750
That's fair. Thank you so much. Thanks.

113
00:06:17,410 --> 00:06:20,920
Oops, looks like when he got the pastry chef, he got you a little bit too.

114
00:06:21,080 --> 00:06:23,540
I paid to have this done.

115
00:06:26,010 --> 00:06:28,050
Love it!

116
00:06:31,050 --> 00:06:32,430
Hey.

117
00:06:31,050 --> 00:06:32,430
Hi.

118
00:06:32,600 --> 00:06:35,060
Oh, you know, uh, Kash really liked you the other day.

119
00:06:35,220 --> 00:06:37,430
He said he thought you were charming.

120
00:06:37,600 --> 00:06:40,850
I thought I was an idiot.

121
00:06:37,600 --> 00:06:40,850
I'm with you.

122
00:06:42,690 --> 00:06:45,570
He asked if you'd go out with him.

123
00:06:42,690 --> 00:06:45,570
Oh!

124
00:06:45,820 --> 00:06:48,190
Oh, I think I'm gonna throw up a little.

125
00:06:48,360 --> 00:06:50,570
What did you say?

126
00:06:48,360 --> 00:06:50,570
I said, "No." Heh.

127
00:06:50,740 --> 00:06:52,530
What?

128
00:06:52,740 --> 00:06:56,700
I figured since you're pregnant, you're not gonna be seeing people.

129
00:06:56,870 --> 00:06:58,750
Okay, Joey.

130
00:06:58,910 --> 00:07:03,500
First of all, Kash Ford? Not people.

131
00:07:03,670 --> 00:07:06,380
Second, what did he say when you told him I was pregnant?

132
00:07:06,550 --> 00:07:09,210
I didn't. I didn't know if you were telling people.

133
00:07:09,380 --> 00:07:12,430
This was back when I thought Kash was still "people."

134
00:07:12,590 --> 00:07:16,390
Good. Don't. Just have him call me.

135
00:07:12,590 --> 00:07:16,390
I really don't think that's such...

136
00:07:16,560 --> 00:07:18,720
Okay, you go do it. I'll come back to that set.

137
00:07:18,890 --> 00:07:21,270
I'll meet more actors. I'll meet them all.

138
00:07:18,890 --> 00:07:21,270
Yup.

139
00:07:23,480 --> 00:07:26,730
Hey, Bob.

140
00:07:23,480 --> 00:07:26,730
Hey! How's my pal Toby doing today?

141
00:07:26,900 --> 00:07:29,360
If I see him, I'll ask.

142
00:07:32,780 --> 00:07:36,490
Hey, Bing. Was that Bob from six you were just talking to?

143
00:07:36,660 --> 00:07:38,490
Yeah.

144
00:07:36,660 --> 00:07:38,490
You know each other?

145
00:07:38,660 --> 00:07:41,120
We're on a semi-first-name basis.

146
00:07:41,710 --> 00:07:43,830
What do you think of adding him to our team?

147
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:46,130
Bob? Ooh.

148
00:07:46,380 --> 00:07:48,880
Working here with us? Every day?

149
00:07:49,050 --> 00:07:51,760
Yeah, I don't know if he has what it takes.

150
00:07:51,920 --> 00:07:55,800
Really? They love him down on six.

151
00:07:51,920 --> 00:07:55,800
But this is 11.

152
00:07:56,600 --> 00:07:59,010
It's almost twice as hard up here.

153
00:07:59,930 --> 00:08:01,430
Okay, I hear you loud and clear.

154
00:08:01,600 --> 00:08:04,020
Bob will stay put.

155
00:08:01,600 --> 00:08:04,020
I think it's best, sir.

156
00:08:04,190 --> 00:08:07,900
We really do need to find somebody. Work is starting to pile up.

157
00:08:08,070 --> 00:08:11,150
I've got a stack of documents on my desk this high.

158
00:08:11,320 --> 00:08:13,490
What you should do, toss them in the shredder...

159
00:08:13,650 --> 00:08:15,200
...and claim you never got them.

160
00:08:16,990 --> 00:08:18,990
That's a good one, Bing.

161
00:08:19,490 --> 00:08:24,040
What does a guy have to do to be taken seriously around here?

162
00:08:28,210 --> 00:08:30,090
Hey.

163
00:08:28,210 --> 00:08:30,090
Okay, I gave him another chance...

164
00:08:30,250 --> 00:08:31,920
...but Tim has got to go.

165
00:08:30,250 --> 00:08:31,920
But...

166
00:08:32,090 --> 00:08:34,130
No! No, no. He's totally incompetent.

167
00:08:34,300 --> 00:08:36,470
I called the chef who recommended him to me.

168
00:08:36,640 --> 00:08:39,010
He said, "Ha, ha! Gotcha!"

169
00:08:40,180 --> 00:08:42,970
Okay, but you can't fire him today.

170
00:08:40,180 --> 00:08:42,970
Why not?

171
00:08:43,140 --> 00:08:47,100
Because I'm dumping him today.

172
00:08:43,140 --> 00:08:47,100
What? You said he was sweet.

173
00:08:47,270 --> 00:08:51,230
He is sweet. He's too sweet. He calls me all the time.

174
00:08:51,400 --> 00:08:54,950
"Did you get home from work okay? Did you get out of the shower okay?"

175
00:08:55,110 --> 00:08:57,990
Just don't pick up your phone.

176
00:08:55,110 --> 00:08:57,990
Then he comes over!

177
00:08:58,160 --> 00:09:01,410
"I was worried about you." Ugh, be a man!

178
00:09:02,080 --> 00:09:04,000
So now I'm not allowed to fire him?

179
00:09:04,160 --> 00:09:07,500
You can't fire him and dump him in the same day. He'll kill himself.

180
00:09:07,670 --> 00:09:10,130
I fire him today, you go out with him another week.

181
00:09:10,290 --> 00:09:14,210
Are you kidding? Another week with that simp, I'll kill myself.

182
00:09:14,380 --> 00:09:17,630
Then we'll both do it today and he'll just have to deal with it.

183
00:09:18,390 --> 00:09:21,100
Okay. But the question is, who's gonna go first?

184
00:09:21,260 --> 00:09:23,310
Whoever goes second is the bitch.

185
00:09:24,390 --> 00:09:26,560
What do you mean?

186
00:09:24,390 --> 00:09:26,560
The boss that fires a guy...

187
00:09:26,730 --> 00:09:28,600
...that's just been dumped? Bitch!

188
00:09:28,770 --> 00:09:31,440
And the woman who dumps a guy that's just been fired?

189
00:09:31,610 --> 00:09:33,530
Blond bitch!

190
00:09:33,690 --> 00:09:36,320
I wanted to do this days ago, so I think I should go first.

191
00:09:37,820 --> 00:09:40,160
Ugh. All right, that makes sense.

192
00:09:40,320 --> 00:09:41,990
Agh, but...

193
00:09:42,160 --> 00:09:45,000
...screw you! I'm going first!

194
00:09:49,420 --> 00:09:51,790
Hey, Toby, you got a sec?

195
00:09:49,420 --> 00:09:51,790
Sure, what's up?

196
00:09:51,960 --> 00:09:55,210
I just had a meeting. I was hoping to get transferred up here.

197
00:09:55,380 --> 00:09:57,170
But I found out it's not gonna happen.

198
00:09:57,340 --> 00:10:01,470
Apparently somebody thinks I'm not "11 th-floor material."

199
00:10:01,970 --> 00:10:05,020
Say, uh, who the hell is this Chandler?

200
00:10:07,850 --> 00:10:11,520
What do you think is the better excuse for why I'm not drinking on this date?

201
00:10:11,690 --> 00:10:15,190
Um, "I'm a recovering alcoholic," "I'm a Mormon"...

202
00:10:15,360 --> 00:10:18,950
...or "I got so hammered last night I'm still a little drunk"?

203
00:10:20,070 --> 00:10:21,200
Hey.

204
00:10:20,070 --> 00:10:21,200
Hi.

205
00:10:21,370 --> 00:10:23,910
So, what do you want to do tonight?

206
00:10:24,080 --> 00:10:27,620
There's a Ukrainian film at the Angelika that's supposed to be very powerful.

207
00:10:27,790 --> 00:10:29,750
Interested?

208
00:10:27,790 --> 00:10:29,750
No. No.

209
00:10:29,920 --> 00:10:32,880
But I'll go see a normal-person movie with you.

210
00:10:33,040 --> 00:10:36,590
Rach, you wanna come?

211
00:10:33,040 --> 00:10:36,590
Oh, no, I can't. I got a date.

212
00:10:37,130 --> 00:10:41,050
Heh. A date?

213
00:10:37,130 --> 00:10:41,050
Yeah. Why, is that weird for you?

214
00:10:41,220 --> 00:10:46,140
Why, no. It's the opposite of weird. It's, uh... It's regular. It's, uh...

215
00:10:46,310 --> 00:10:50,440
It's mundane. It's actually a little dull.

216
00:10:50,600 --> 00:10:53,520
It's no Ukrainian film, I'll tell you.

217
00:10:53,690 --> 00:10:55,900
Ooh! Earrings!

218
00:10:56,610 --> 00:11:02,410
A date? She's got a date? With who?

219
00:10:56,610 --> 00:11:02,410
I set her up with this actor on my show.

220
00:11:02,570 --> 00:11:06,450
You set her up?

221
00:11:02,570 --> 00:11:06,450
No.

222
00:11:07,450 --> 00:11:10,540
Joey, what were you thinking?

223
00:11:07,450 --> 00:11:10,540
That it would probably be okay...

224
00:11:10,710 --> 00:11:13,750
...because Ross hasn't gone out with Rachel in five years.

225
00:11:13,920 --> 00:11:16,880
Joey, I'm not worried about her. I'm worried about my baby.

226
00:11:17,050 --> 00:11:19,630
Whoever she dates, my baby dates.

227
00:11:19,800 --> 00:11:24,430
Where is this "actor" taking them?

228
00:11:19,800 --> 00:11:24,430
Hey! I'm an "actor" too.

229
00:11:26,810 --> 00:11:28,610
I'm not sure. I think they're taking the ferry

230
00:11:28,810 --> 00:11:30,810
to some Italian place on Staten Island.

231
00:11:30,980 --> 00:11:34,690
A ferry? My baby's going on a ferry?

232
00:11:34,860 --> 00:11:37,190
Do you have any idea how dangerous those are?

233
00:11:37,360 --> 00:11:41,530
Aren't we talking about those big boats that go, like, five miles an hour?

234
00:11:41,700 --> 00:11:44,610
Why don't they just jump out of an airplane? That's a fun date.

235
00:11:44,780 --> 00:11:46,620
Or burn each other with matches? That's fun too.

236
00:11:46,780 --> 00:11:48,160
Whoo!

237
00:11:51,660 --> 00:11:53,000
Hey, Joey.

238
00:11:51,660 --> 00:11:53,000
Hey, Kash.

239
00:11:53,170 --> 00:11:55,420
Uh, hey, Ross, this is Kash.

240
00:11:53,170 --> 00:11:55,420
Hey.

241
00:11:55,580 --> 00:11:58,960
Hey, I hear you're going on a ferry tonight.

242
00:11:55,580 --> 00:11:58,960
Yeah.

243
00:11:59,130 --> 00:12:01,460
Bit of a daredevil, are we?

244
00:12:02,970 --> 00:12:06,140
Hey, you guys, do you think this is too slutty? Hi, Kash.

245
00:12:06,850 --> 00:12:10,390
Hey, Rachel. You ready to go?

246
00:12:06,850 --> 00:12:10,390
Yeah. See you guys later.

247
00:12:10,560 --> 00:12:13,690
Okay. Have a great time, you guys.

248
00:12:10,560 --> 00:12:13,690
Thank you.

249
00:12:13,850 --> 00:12:16,600
And yes, it is too slutty!

250
00:12:23,820 --> 00:12:25,780
Hi.

251
00:12:23,820 --> 00:12:25,780
Ah!

252
00:12:26,320 --> 00:12:27,410
Hi.

253
00:12:27,580 --> 00:12:31,040
I'm so glad you called. I feel like it's always me calling you.

254
00:12:31,200 --> 00:12:34,870
So, what's up? Is everything okay with Phoebe?

255
00:12:36,210 --> 00:12:39,670
It will be in a minute. Listen.

256
00:12:39,840 --> 00:12:43,340
Tim, you're a really great guy.

257
00:12:39,840 --> 00:12:43,340
That's because I'm with you.

258
00:12:48,100 --> 00:12:51,430
I'm just... I'm in a place in my life right now where I...

259
00:12:53,180 --> 00:12:55,270
Whoops! So sorry. "This just in." Heh.

260
00:12:57,650 --> 00:13:00,360
It's 911 from the restaurant. That means Monica needs me.

261
00:13:00,520 --> 00:13:03,070
Oh, no, she doesn't! I know what that is. You can stay.

262
00:13:03,280 --> 00:13:04,740
Aw...

263
00:13:04,900 --> 00:13:07,280
I'll miss you too, Pheebs.

264
00:13:07,950 --> 00:13:12,290
And I will be holding you right here.

265
00:13:20,130 --> 00:13:23,460
So, what movie do you wanna see? And not another one I have to read.

266
00:13:23,630 --> 00:13:25,550
I get enough of that from books.

267
00:13:27,640 --> 00:13:30,850
Books?

268
00:13:27,640 --> 00:13:30,850
All right, car magazines, cereal boxes...

269
00:13:31,010 --> 00:13:32,640
...but it's, like, enough!

270
00:13:33,560 --> 00:13:35,230
I tell you what, why don't we...?

271
00:13:35,390 --> 00:13:38,060
Why don't we stay. Let's not see a movie. We'll just hang.

272
00:13:38,230 --> 00:13:41,110
Just wait for Rachel to come back from her date?

273
00:13:41,270 --> 00:13:44,610
Hey, if that's what you wanna do, I'm not gonna say no.

274
00:13:44,820 --> 00:13:47,530
Dude, what is going on?

275
00:13:47,700 --> 00:13:51,160
I just... I have to find out how it went.

276
00:13:47,700 --> 00:13:51,160
Why?

277
00:13:51,330 --> 00:13:53,410
This guy could be my baby's stepfather.

278
00:13:53,580 --> 00:13:56,620
They go on one date and you're worried about them getting married?

279
00:13:56,790 --> 00:13:59,000
He's not you.

280
00:13:59,750 --> 00:14:03,210
I just, I can't believe she's dating.

281
00:14:03,380 --> 00:14:07,260
What did you think she was gonna do?

282
00:14:03,380 --> 00:14:07,260
I don't know.

283
00:14:07,840 --> 00:14:10,720
I guess I can't believe any of this is happening.

284
00:14:11,430 --> 00:14:12,600
What do you mean?

285
00:14:12,760 --> 00:14:15,770
I always thought when I had another kid, it'd be different.

286
00:14:17,770 --> 00:14:23,060
I love Ben. But every time I drop him off at Carol and Susan's...

287
00:14:23,230 --> 00:14:26,530
...it breaks my heart a little.

288
00:14:27,190 --> 00:14:31,660
I've always had this picture of me and my next wife in bed on Sunday.

289
00:14:31,820 --> 00:14:36,830
My kid comes running in, leaps up on the bed and we all read the paper together.

290
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:41,120
You know? Maybe fight over the science section.

291
00:14:41,790 --> 00:14:44,340
That's a nice picture. Maybe you can still have that.

292
00:14:44,500 --> 00:14:48,170
No, I can't. Rachel's out with some guy.

293
00:14:48,340 --> 00:14:50,720
My baby went with her.

294
00:14:52,180 --> 00:14:55,890
If anything, that picture keeps moving further away.

295
00:14:57,470 --> 00:14:59,640
Hey, can I ask you something?

296
00:14:59,810 --> 00:15:06,020
In this picture of you and your wife, is your wife Rachel?

297
00:15:06,860 --> 00:15:08,780
It used to be.

298
00:15:10,280 --> 00:15:13,410
Now she doesn't really have a face.

299
00:15:14,660 --> 00:15:17,370
Smoking body, though.

300
00:15:18,950 --> 00:15:24,130
Good call. But the face, Ross, the face isn't Rachel.

301
00:15:24,290 --> 00:15:28,420
No. But, ugh, how much easier would it be if it were?

302
00:15:28,590 --> 00:15:30,760
I know, but I don't think that's what she wants.

303
00:15:30,930 --> 00:15:32,260
It's not what I want either.

304
00:15:32,430 --> 00:15:35,010
And I can't force myself to fall in love with her again.

305
00:15:35,180 --> 00:15:38,010
Ross, maybe you need a new picture.

306
00:15:38,180 --> 00:15:42,980
Okay? It's not gonna be what you thought. But no matter what...

307
00:15:43,150 --> 00:15:46,940
...there's gonna be a brand-new little baby. Your baby.

308
00:15:47,900 --> 00:15:50,650
Who cares what the picture looks like?

309
00:15:51,740 --> 00:15:53,400
Yeah.

310
00:15:54,320 --> 00:15:57,370
Hey, tell you what. Let's you and me go out and have some fun.

311
00:15:57,530 --> 00:16:00,240
Huh? Whatever you want. Come on.

312
00:16:01,370 --> 00:16:04,710
We can catch that Ukrainian film.

313
00:16:01,370 --> 00:16:04,710
No, I said fun.

314
00:16:07,670 --> 00:16:09,420
Hey, Toby?

315
00:16:07,670 --> 00:16:09,420
Hey, Bobby.

316
00:16:09,880 --> 00:16:11,050
It's Bob, actually.

317
00:16:13,340 --> 00:16:17,220
You work up here. Can you tell me where Chandler Bing's office is?

318
00:16:17,390 --> 00:16:21,850
Uh, yeah, it's right...

319
00:16:23,270 --> 00:16:25,940
Right there. Let me ask you, why?

320
00:16:26,110 --> 00:16:28,940
Ha, ha, I wanna talk to that bastard, see what his problem is.

321
00:16:29,110 --> 00:16:31,190
Okay, Bob, listen. Uh...

322
00:16:32,490 --> 00:16:35,410
I'm the reason you didn't get the job.

323
00:16:35,570 --> 00:16:37,490
Toby, don't.

324
00:16:35,570 --> 00:16:37,490
Bob.

325
00:16:37,660 --> 00:16:42,160
Toby, I'm not gonna let you cover for him.

326
00:16:42,330 --> 00:16:45,920
Anything you say will just get me more upset with Chandler.

327
00:16:47,130 --> 00:16:49,590
Well that puts me in a difficult position.

328
00:16:53,050 --> 00:16:56,590
I got your page. Is everything okay?

329
00:16:53,050 --> 00:16:56,590
Uh, well, that depends.

330
00:16:56,760 --> 00:17:00,640
How are things with Phoebe?

331
00:16:56,760 --> 00:17:00,640
It's great. Thank you for introducing us.

332
00:17:00,810 --> 00:17:05,060
Oh, my pleasure. Okay, I'm afraid I've got some bad news.

333
00:17:06,100 --> 00:17:08,150
Phoebe!

334
00:17:06,100 --> 00:17:08,150
Monica!

335
00:17:09,650 --> 00:17:11,650
I'm breaking up with you!

336
00:17:09,650 --> 00:17:11,650
You're fired!

337
00:17:11,820 --> 00:17:14,650
What?

338
00:17:11,820 --> 00:17:14,650
I'm breaking up with you.

339
00:17:14,820 --> 00:17:18,110
You're fired.

340
00:17:14,820 --> 00:17:18,110
Why?

341
00:17:18,280 --> 00:17:22,540
I'm sorry. I'm not ready for a relationship right now.

342
00:17:22,700 --> 00:17:27,210
And I'm sorry too. But, well, I like things done a certain way.

343
00:17:27,370 --> 00:17:32,670
And the chemistry's just not right.

344
00:17:27,370 --> 00:17:32,670
Ooh, good. The chemistry thing for us too.

345
00:17:34,210 --> 00:17:38,260
Wow, heh. Um, okay. Um...

346
00:17:39,260 --> 00:17:41,680
I realize I came on a little strong.

347
00:17:41,850 --> 00:17:44,430
But it's only because I think you're so amazing.

348
00:17:45,480 --> 00:17:46,730
And, uh...

349
00:17:47,230 --> 00:17:51,020
I just wanna tell you how much I appreciate you giving me an opportunity here...

350
00:17:51,190 --> 00:17:54,530
...because you're the most talented chef I've ever worked for.

351
00:17:56,280 --> 00:17:58,200
Anyway, heh.

352
00:18:04,040 --> 00:18:07,330
Tim, wait. Wait. Um...

353
00:18:04,040 --> 00:18:07,330
Yeah?

354
00:18:08,290 --> 00:18:12,960
I think I spoke too quickly. There's a learning curve with this job.

355
00:18:13,130 --> 00:18:15,760
Maybe we could try it again.

356
00:18:13,130 --> 00:18:15,760
Really?

357
00:18:15,920 --> 00:18:17,010
Thank you so much.

358
00:18:17,170 --> 00:18:19,130
Because I know I can be better.

359
00:18:17,170 --> 00:18:19,130
Okay.

360
00:18:21,350 --> 00:18:25,010
And Tim, I just want to say good luck here.

361
00:18:32,730 --> 00:18:34,980
Hello. Ha, ha.

362
00:18:32,730 --> 00:18:34,980
Hi.

363
00:18:35,150 --> 00:18:36,940
Uh, how was the date?

364
00:18:37,110 --> 00:18:43,320
Well, I'm alone and I just bought $15 worth of candy bars. What do you think?

365
00:18:43,490 --> 00:18:45,740
Huh. What happened?

366
00:18:43,490 --> 00:18:45,740
Made the mistake...

367
00:18:45,910 --> 00:18:48,120
...of telling him that I was pregnant.

368
00:18:48,290 --> 00:18:52,540
He didn't, uh, take it so well?

369
00:18:48,290 --> 00:18:52,540
Well, better than you.

370
00:18:53,250 --> 00:18:56,460
But still not what you want.

371
00:18:53,250 --> 00:18:56,460
Oh?

372
00:18:56,630 --> 00:19:00,300
Yeah. He got all weird and sputtery. Then he said, uh:

373
00:19:00,470 --> 00:19:03,470
"I hear those hemorrhoids are a bitch."

374
00:19:04,010 --> 00:19:06,640
He sounds swell.

375
00:19:04,010 --> 00:19:06,640
Doesn't he?

376
00:19:07,560 --> 00:19:09,520
Hey, you want a little cheering up?

377
00:19:09,690 --> 00:19:12,060
Yes. Okay.

378
00:19:09,690 --> 00:19:12,060
Sit down.

379
00:19:13,150 --> 00:19:15,770
Guess whose middle name is Muriel?

380
00:19:20,450 --> 00:19:22,410
Chandler M. Bing.

381
00:19:20,450 --> 00:19:22,410
Yu-huh.

382
00:19:22,570 --> 00:19:24,410
Oh, my God.

383
00:19:28,790 --> 00:19:31,870
I'm sorry about your date.

384
00:19:28,790 --> 00:19:31,870
It's all right.

385
00:19:32,120 --> 00:19:35,250
I guess I'm just done with the whole dating thing.

386
00:19:35,790 --> 00:19:40,260
Just one more thing in my life that is suddenly completely different.

387
00:19:40,510 --> 00:19:43,930
This is hard.

388
00:19:40,510 --> 00:19:43,930
Yeah, I know.

389
00:19:46,350 --> 00:19:48,680
On the other hand, in, um...

390
00:19:48,850 --> 00:19:52,520
In about seven months you're gonna have something...

391
00:19:52,690 --> 00:19:57,270
...that you're gonna love more than any guy you've ever gone out with.

392
00:19:59,480 --> 00:20:02,360
Just wait. Wait until, uh...

393
00:20:02,910 --> 00:20:06,450
Wait until the first time your baby grabs your finger.

394
00:20:07,620 --> 00:20:09,120
You have no idea.

395
00:20:11,500 --> 00:20:14,000
Thanks, sweetie.

396
00:20:17,840 --> 00:20:23,630
You wanna grab some coffee?

397
00:20:17,840 --> 00:20:23,630
No. I'm gonna go eat 10 candy bars.

398
00:20:23,880 --> 00:20:25,840
I thought I cheered you up.

399
00:20:23,880 --> 00:20:25,840
Oh, you did.

400
00:20:26,010 --> 00:20:28,600
There are 20 in here.

401
00:20:26,010 --> 00:20:28,600
Right.

402
00:20:29,510 --> 00:20:31,930
Good night.

403
00:20:29,510 --> 00:20:31,930
Good night.

404
00:20:39,230 --> 00:20:40,400
Ross?

405
00:20:39,230 --> 00:20:40,400
Yeah?

406
00:20:40,570 --> 00:20:43,070
Hey, it's Mona. From the wedding.

407
00:20:43,240 --> 00:20:45,820
Oh, hi!

408
00:20:43,240 --> 00:20:45,820
Hi.

409
00:20:45,990 --> 00:20:47,200
Wow, uh...

410
00:20:47,370 --> 00:20:49,490
How are you?

411
00:20:47,370 --> 00:20:49,490
I'm good, except, um...

412
00:20:49,660 --> 00:20:51,290
...you still owe me a dance.

413
00:20:51,450 --> 00:20:52,950
Oh, that's right.

414
00:20:51,450 --> 00:20:52,950
Mm.

415
00:20:53,120 --> 00:20:56,170
Well, uh, would you be interested in seeing a Ukrainian film?

416
00:20:58,460 --> 00:21:00,380
Oh, you're serious. Sure.

417
00:21:01,880 --> 00:21:04,170
Great. Well, uh...

418
00:21:05,180 --> 00:21:07,390
I think I might need one more cup of coffee.

419
00:21:07,550 --> 00:21:10,720
Sure, uh, let me get it for you.

420
00:21:07,550 --> 00:21:10,720
Okay.

421
00:21:28,570 --> 00:21:31,160
Bob? Bob!

422
00:21:31,580 --> 00:21:32,830
Bob!

423
00:21:33,910 --> 00:21:38,580
What the hell are you doing?

424
00:21:33,910 --> 00:21:38,580
I just found out this is Chandler's office.

425
00:21:38,750 --> 00:21:40,670
Come on, Toby. Give me a hand!

